/**
 * Deterministic demo workspace used for portfolio screenshots.
 *
 *   pnpm --filter @phiguard/web seed:demo
 *
 * Unlike `dev-seed.ts` — which creates the minimum needed to log in — this
 * builds a clinic that has been running for months: three locations, all five
 * RBAC roles, work in every state, incidents mid-triage, a partly-completed
 * compliance program, and a real audit trail.
 *
 * Every value is generated by `@faker-js/faker` under a fixed seed, so runs are
 * reproducible and no real person's data can end up in a screenshot. Nothing
 * here is or resembles PHI: the records describe clinic operations and
 * workforce compliance, never patients.
 *
 * Mutations go through the domain libraries (`createTask`, `createIncident`,
 * `transitionIncident`, `completeItem`, ...) rather than raw inserts wherever
 * the library supports the end state. That is deliberate: those helpers write
 * audit events, so the seeded audit log is genuine rather than fabricated.
 */
